<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Landrecies</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Landrecies is a small town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sambre">Sambre</a> in the Nord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, formerly part of the County of Hainaut. A fortified frontier town, it was besieged repeatedly in the wars between France and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> and passed to France by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-the-pyrenees">Treaty of the Pyrenees</a> in 1659. It was besieged again in 1712 and in 1794.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/landrecies.jpg" alt="Landrecies" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Havang(nl) · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Landrecies_(Nord,_Fr)_Hotel_de_ville_et_statue_Dupleix.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
